Third-Party Components
-----------------------

The following third-party tools and dependencies retain their own
licenses and are not covered by Kairon DFIR's own AGPL-3.0 license
grant. Review each one's license terms independently before building
or redistributing a Kairon DFIR image or artifact that bundles them.

- Eric Zimmerman Tools are downloaded during the backend Docker build
  and are not vendored in this repository.
- MemProcFS (Ulf Frisk, https://github.com/ufrisk/MemProcFS) is
  downloaded from its pinned release during the memory-worker Docker
  build (SHA-256 checked) and used for Find Evil. Its vmm.so is rebuilt
  from the release's source with the patches in
  docker/memory-worker/patches/ (a fix for a lookup that never ends on
  Windows 11+); see docker/memory-worker/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. It is
  licensed under AGPL-3.0; its bundled components carry their own
  licenses (license_*.txt in the release, copied to
  /licenses/memprocfs in the image). Its built-in Elastic YARA rules
  (Elastic License 2.0) are not enabled.
- Volatility 3 (Volatility Foundation) is installed in the
  memory-worker image and is licensed under the Volatility Software
  License.
- OpenSearch, PostgreSQL, Redis, FastAPI, React, and other runtime and
  build dependencies retain their own licenses; see each project's own
  repository for terms.

See SECURITY.md for further detail on third-party tooling and
deployment security guidance.
